<section class="architecture-notes" aria-label="Four architecture takeaways">
  <dl class="architecture-notes__grid">
    <div>
      <dt><span>Generation</span>One LLM, two jobs</dt>
      <dd><strong>LangChain generates answers.</strong> Hindsight uses Muse Glimmer to <strong>extract facts</strong> during ingestion.</dd>
      <dd>The same local model serves both roles here; each role has its own configuration.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><span>Retrieval</span>Separate models find the evidence</dt>
      <dd><strong>Embeddings</strong> represent meaning numerically. A <strong>reranker</strong> rescores candidate memories.</dd>
      <dd>This sample uses the container defaults for both. Choosing the chat model does not configure retrieval models.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><span>Persistence</span>Memory survives agent restarts</dt>
      <dd><strong>Storage holds durable memory.</strong> Restarting the Python agent does not erase it.</dd>
      <dd>The <strong>control plane</strong> is an inspection UI; it is not required in every answer path.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt><span>Orchestration</span>The engine runs memory operations</dt>
      <dd><strong>Retain</strong> ingests, <strong>recall</strong> searches, and <strong>reflect</strong> reasons over evidence.</dd>
      <dd>The API dispatches these operations to the memory engine. Workers can handle background ingestion and consolidation.</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
  <aside class="architecture-notes__scope" aria-label="Local example configuration">
    <strong>In this local example</strong>
    <p>Writes wait for ingestion to finish. Observations and automatic consolidation are disabled, so the first experiment focuses on storing and retrieving facts.</p>
  </aside>
</section>

